Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraFiberBundleQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"d62009ee-c978-4033-b7e5-53c50991fceb"],

Cell["LLM generated.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f78b9e4-0b9f-4f5a-b48b-3db8f0c28354"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"6c502f44-2be3-4dc4-93c9-fd3fd81563b3"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraFiberBundleQ"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberBundleQ", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["fib", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6739f368-5d06-47df-94c9-24e08a0de30c"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "tests whether ",
 StyleBox["fib", "TI"],
 " has a common fiber graph and an adjacency-preserving matching over every \
base edge.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"ca2ebbea-810c-4b81-98c6-64fa36395a61"],

Cell["\<\
The fibers must be mutually isomorphic, including across disconnected base \
components.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b016fa2a-83e2-4407-a757-c7bbc76148d2"],

Cell["\<\
Every total vertex has exactly one transverse neighbour over each adjacent \
base vertex. Each resulting fiber bijection preserves vertical adjacency.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"92046a57-0731-4853-9e88-5cad4c08e0e5"],

Cell["\<\
This is the finite Cartesian graph-bundle condition. The inverse image of a \
base edge is a Cartesian product of that edge with the common fiber, \
respecting the projection.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"51f1670d-e0d1-4752-88b3-a3a3c36e62be"],

Cell["\<\
No topology or higher-dimensional cells are supplied by the predicate.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"da8ff054-57aa-4a2f-91fe-3cdaee26c595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Twisted coverings with a common sheet count are bundles. Trivial monodromy \
is a separate question, tested for a selected connection by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFlatConnectionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFlatConnectionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3812fddb-bcf7-4b9b-89c3-2f3746a54a49"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c0311b08-42c1-48a4-9dea-dbdcf399147a"],

Cell["\<\
A covering may have different sheet counts on disconnected base components; \
such a covering is not a bundle with one common fiber.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"00a10635-b77a-48f3-bbc6-7c4df03a85a9"],

Cell["\<\
A nonempty list is tested by conjunction. An empty list is False; the empty \
fibered graph is a bundle. Unsupported inputs remain unevaluated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0ca9d39b-bc19-45ac-8f3a-7827b1b6f407"]
}, Open  ]],

